implementationPlan.description:
Reopen 3. QA qa-ba3f4f35 failed DoD 1 on the INVERSE UNC case. Read first:
- rejectionDetails;
- task comments 09feee65, 51a169fb and e8181ee2;
- the Serena notes decision-protected-windows-alias-refusal and gotcha-windows-node-namespaced-realpath.

The leak: getWorkspacePath returns uri.fsPath unchanged. For a base \\localhost\C$\...\project (also 127.0.0.1, or a mapped drive whose real path is UNC), realpath keeps the UNC form. The local C:\...\project spelling of the SAME folder then compares as outside: isOutsideProject keeps it in PATH, and selectInstalledFile accepts a node inside it.

The fix (step 2) stops enumerating spellings: on a Windows host, only plain local drive paths are compared, on BOTH sides. The architect validated this exact diff on native Windows; it is in D:\moe-rf06b-r3-architect-probe\vscode (the patched source, the test file and six mutants). That folder and QA's folders (D:\qa-rf06b-r2, D:\qa-rf06b-ba3f4f35-wwdawo_j) are read-only for you.

TESTS FIRST, in moe-vscode/tests/protected-daemon-spawn.test.cjs. Keep every other line byte-identical; copy the probe file's lines. The spellings below are in Windows notation; write them as escaped JS literals, as the probe file does.

(a) In the test 'Windows alias predicate…':
- append to the true list: \x, /x, C:x, x, \\?\Volume{0}\x, \\?\GLOBALROOT\Device\HarddiskVolume3\x and \\.\pipe\x;
- append //?/c:/x to the false list.
Do NOT list \\.\C:\x as false: its '.' device segment was already an alias under the reopen-2 rule.

(b) Directly after the test 'Windows aliases cannot run project executables…', add the probe's 19-line test 'Windows alias project bases prove nothing outside them and start no daemon', skipped off Windows like its neighbours. Setup:
- reason = 'the project directory is not a plain local Windows path';
- copy whoami.exe to p\moe-rf06b-base.exe;
- control: a bare-name spawnSync with PATH = p from cwd f.outside exits 0;
- write p + '.\.moe\project.json' (Node's namespaced mkdir creates a literal 'project.' folder), plus a junction f.outside\dot-project pointing to it;
- MOE_NODE_COMMAND = a node.exe inside p.
For each base of [\\localhost\<d>$<rest of p>, \\127.0.0.1\<d>$<rest of p>, the junction, p.slice(2)]:
- isOutsideProject(p, base) and isOutsideProject(f.outside, base) are both false;
- installedExecutable(node, base) is rejected with reason;
- protectedDaemonEnvironment({ PATH: [p, f.outside].join(';'), SystemRoot }, base, f.node, true, undefined).PATH is '', and the bare-name spawn with that env gives ENOENT;
- await f.client.startDaemon('start', base) for every base except the rooted one.
At the end, f.spawns is [] and f.errors is exactly three refusal(reason) messages.

Why each base:
- The UNC bases are QA's repro. The raw spelling refuses them, so the result does not depend on the admin share being reachable: an unreachable share fails lstat with code UNKNOWN, and runtimeProfile then fails closed to protected.
- The junction stands in for a mapped drive (a plain spelling whose real path is an alias). It is the only base that exercises the real-path checks.
- The rooted base resolves against the host cwd drive, while the daemon would resolve it against ITS cwd drive. It skips startDaemon because runtimeProfile can read legacy there.
The fixture's fs.rmSync removes the literal folder and the junction; the probe left no moe-rf06b-* temp dirs.

RED evidence, record both:
- Linux `cd moe-vscode && node --test tests/protected-daemon-spawn.test.cjs` fails (a) at '\x'.
- `cmd.exe /d /c "cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-vscode && node --test tests/protected-daemon-spawn.test.cjs"` fails (a), and (b) with isOutsideProject [true, true] for the localhost base.
The architect saw both red on e83fef4c.

Implement in moe-vscode/src/services/MoeDaemonClient.ts. These are exactly the probe's three edits (net +2 lines). Add no import, and change nothing else.

1. isWindowsAlias becomes an allow-list. Keep the same signature and host default, and replace only the UNC clause:
   return windows && (/[. ](?:[\\/]|$)/.test(p) || !/^[A-Za-z]:\//.test(comparablePath(p, false)));
   Doc comment: /** On Windows only plain drive paths compare: Win32 strips segment-ending dots/spaces Node's \\?\ fs keeps; UNC, device and rooted forms can name any folder. */
   comparablePath strips a \\?\ prefix (so \\?\C:\x stays local) and maps \\?\UNC\ to //.

2. isOutsideProject:
   if (!isFullyQualified(p) || isWindowsAlias(basePath)) { return false; }
   const forms = pathForms(p), projects = pathForms(basePath);
   if ([...forms, ...projects].some(form => isWindowsAlias(form))) { return false; }
   The comparison line is unchanged. The raw base is checked before any I/O, so an unreachable share costs nothing per PATH entry. Unequal namespaces never prove 'outside'.

3. selectInstalledFile. As its first lines:
   const notLocal = 'the project directory is not a plain local Windows path';
   if (isWindowsAlias(basePath)) { return { rejected: notLocal }; }
   Then the existing realpath, null check and rejected helper, followed by:
   if (isWindowsAlias(project)) { return rejected(notLocal, project); }
   Checking the spelling before realpath gives a reachable share, an unreachable share and a rooted spelling the same reason.

Error handling is unchanged:
- isOutsideProject's try/catch still answers false for non-ENOENT realpath errors, e.g. UNKNOWN for an unreachable share.
- The UI reason is path-free, and the log gets the real path through rejected().
- startProtectedDaemon needs no edit: the daemon's installedArtifact refuses first, so it shows 'Protected execution profile: the project directory is not a plain local Windows path. Project and PATH copies of the Moe daemon are not used.' and spawns nothing.
- RF06's AgentLauncher gets the same refusal.

Always call the predicate through an arrow, never as forms.some(isWindowsAlias), and never pass the windows argument at call sites (host semantics).
POSIX and legacy are unchanged. Step 1's tests now pass on Linux and on native Windows.

Load adversarial-self-review. Review only the reopen-3 diff, `git diff e83fef4c -- moe-vscode/`. Check:
(a) QA's UNC bases, a junction or mapped-drive base, a rooted base and every reopen-1/2 spelling are refused.
(b) Nothing ordinary is newly refused: C:\, C:\Program Files\nodejs\, Python3.11, \\?\C:\ forms, 8.3 names and subst drives (realpath maps a subst drive to the local path; architect probe).
(c) POSIX is unchanged (the Linux run). The legacy spawn bytes are unchanged, there is no new import, process.env is never mutated, and UI messages carry no path.
(d) Each of these six mutants is killed by an assertion. Run them on scratch copies only (see D:\moe-rf06b-r3-architect-probe\vscode\mutants):
- drop the raw-basePath check in isOutsideProject;
- drop ...projects from its alias check;
- drop the raw-basePath check in selectInstalledFile;
- drop the project real-path check there;
- restore the old clause comparablePath(p, false).startsWith('//');
- ignore the windows parameter.

Report in the completion summary:
- Size, from `git diff --numstat 0645f5e3^ -- moe-vscode/`. The probe measures +462/-3, net 459. The ceiling is the CQ-RF06b rail in get_context allRails.epic at completion time: 460 today. MODIFY_RAIL prop-27ddd22a proposes 470, and the governor decides it. Stay at or below the active value, and quote it.
- Accepted cost: under protected on Windows, a workspace on a UNC path, a mapped drive or \\wsl$ starts no daemon or agent.
- VS Code is stricter than JetBrains until twin task-526a2080 lands.
- Still out of scope (QA-accepted, shared with JetBrains): a not-yet-existing PATH leaf below a symlink, junction, 8.3, subst or mapped-drive ancestor is compared lexically. Running-daemon provenance stays with CQ-RF07.

comments.content:
@governor-693b7073 Rev 3 is submitted (planRevision 3, TURBO, WORKING). It takes your second direction: fail closed outside one namespace, with no further spelling enumeration. On a Windows host, isWindowsAlias becomes an allow-list (plain local drive path), and it applies to the project base too (raw, resolved and real forms) as well as to candidates.
I validated the exact diff on native Windows (D:\moe-rf06b-r3-architect-probe):
- the new tests are red on e83fef4c and green with the patch;
- all six mutants are killed;
- QA's trailing-dot, aliases and unc-project repros report NO LEAK, kept:false and UNC_PROJECT_LEAKS=0;
- the full suite is green on both hosts, apart from scratch-only ESLint rows.
Size: +462/-3, net 459 from 0645f5e3^. That is 1 under the active 460, and the current wording covers only the reopen-2/UNC growth. I filed MODIFY_RAIL prop-27ddd22a (EPIC): ceiling 470, with the alias definition extended to the reopen-3 base forms. Please decide it before QA reviews; the worker is told to stay at or below whatever allRails.epic shows at completion.
Still out of scope and QA-accepted: not-yet-existing PATH leaves under link, 8.3, subst or mapped ancestors. Identity (dev+ino) containment would close those, but it needs a rewrite and its own SMB probe, so it is left for later hardening.
